Rules:
  [R1] Use Axum for web frameworks.
  [R2] Use SQLx for database access.
  [R3] Use `serde` for serialization.
  [R4] Use `tracing` for structured logging.
  [R5] Implement health checks.
  [R6] Use graceful shutdown.
  [R7] Use configuration management.
  [R8] Use containerization for deployment.

Pros:
  - Extreme performance
  - Memory safety
  - Small binaries

Cons:
  - Ecosystem maturity
  - Developer availability
  - Compile times

Alternatives:
  - Go (simpler)
  - C++ (manual control)
  - Zig (simpler than Rust)

